  "slug": "quantum-contact-1adc",
  "summary": "Recent preprints report quantized superconducting transport, bosonic phase fluctuations in moiré graphene, and fermion-induced frustration in Josephson arrays.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a focus on superconducting phase coherence in engineered or confined systems, although the platforms differ. A gate-tunable superconducting quantum point contact in Ge/SiGe, probed via a SQUID, shows conductance and switching current with correlated quantization. A moiré flatband superconductor in alternating twisted trilayer graphene is examined through quantum phase fluctuations linking superconductivity and bosonic phases. In odd-parity Josephson trijunction arrays, trapped fermions induce frustration that maps onto a Kagome XY antiferromagnet with 6e phase coherence. What is new in these preprints is the explicit link between microscopic superconducting constraints and effective quantized, bosonic, or spin-like descriptions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
